WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.985
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Brocard Axis is the central line connecting the Circumcenter X three and the Symmedian Point X six.

2
00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:15.170
It serves as the line of symmetry of the Brocard configuration and is perpendicular to the Lemoine axis.

3
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:22.857
Because the three Apollonian circles have their centers on the Lemoine axis, their common radical chord is the Brocard axis.

4
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:32.000
The two intersection points of all three Apollonian circles—the First and Second Isodynamic Points X fifteen and X sixteen—lie directly on the Brocard axis.

5
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:44.620
Segment X three X six is the diameter of the Brocard circle, while X fifteen and X sixteen are mutual inverses in the circumcircle and harmonic conjugates with respect to the Apollonian structure along the Brocard axis.
